WEBVTT

00:12:22.482 --> 00:12:24.105
Dad wants us to pick up
where he left off.

00:12:24.106 --> 00:12:26.178
Saving people, hunting things.

00:12:26.179 --> 00:12:27.490
The family business.

00:12:29.497 --> 00:12:31.543
You still running credit-card scams?

00:12:31.544 --> 00:12:32.935
You think credit-card fraud is easy?

00:12:32.936 --> 00:12:35.035
- Okay, Mr. Burkowitz.
- Federal marshals.

00:12:35.036 --> 00:12:36.942
- Environmental study majors.
- I'm father Simmons.

00:12:36.943 --> 00:12:38.837
U.S. Wildlife service.
Nigel Tuffnel.

00:12:38.838 --> 00:12:41.643
- Dr. Jerry Kaplan. Art dealers. Rangers.
- Reporters. Students.

00:12:41.647 --> 00:12:44.762
- Fraternity brothers.
- Homeland security? Pretty illegal, even for us.

00:12:44.763 --> 00:12:47.548
<i>S.W.A.T. team discovered
a local woman bound and gagged.</i>

00:12:47.551 --> 00:12:51.509
<i>Her attacker, a white male
approximately 24 to 30 years of age,</i>

00:12:51.504 --> 00:12:54.088
- <i>was discovered hiding in the home.</i>
- Shapeshifter?

00:12:54.121 --> 00:12:56.165
Every culture in the world
has a shapeshifter lore,

00:12:56.168 --> 00:12:59.573
legends of creatures who can transform
themselves into animals or other men.

00:13:04.898 --> 00:13:08.975
Cops are blaming this Dean Winchester guy
for Emily's murder.

00:13:09.009 --> 00:13:10.794
- Sorry I'm gonna miss it.
- Miss what?

00:13:10.859 --> 00:13:13.164
How many chances am I gonna have
to see my own funeral?

00:13:25.457 --> 00:13:26.455
Under what name?

00:13:27.179 --> 00:13:29.815
Oh, yeah, that's my favorite so far.

00:13:30.727 --> 00:13:33.213
Possible I.D.S in three states
that we know of.

00:13:36.849 --> 00:13:38.152
I got to call you back.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:46.352
Wow.

00:13:49.319 --> 00:13:51.724
First I thought
you were just stepping up your game.

00:13:52.697 --> 00:13:53.903
Credit-card fraud,

00:13:54.508 --> 00:13:56.724
breaking and entering.
This one,

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.032
a puzzle...

00:13:58.439 --> 00:13:59.925
Grave desecration.

00:14:01.558 --> 00:14:04.574
But still, these are a long way from murder.

00:14:05.799 --> 00:14:07.764
Then we get a fax from St. Louis...

00:14:09.547 --> 00:14:13.032
where you're suspected of torturing
and murdering a young woman.

00:14:14.069 --> 00:14:16.773
However, no one could prove anything,
of course, because

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.535
supposedly you died there.

00:14:21.897 --> 00:14:23.463
But I got to tell you something.

00:14:25.099 --> 00:14:27.285
You look pretty healthy to me.

00:14:30.879 --> 00:14:34.545
So, now we know Karen Giles
wasn't the first person you murdered.

00:14:34.998 --> 00:14:37.114
Going somewhere, Sam?

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.852
But I guarantee you she's the last.

00:14:50.278 --> 00:14:51.782
Transcript : Raceman

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.335
Titelilie
www.forom.com

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:05.095
Thought you might be thirsty.

00:15:05.097 --> 00:15:06.704
Okay, so you're the good cop.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.555
- Where's the bad cop?
- He's with your brother.

00:15:10.558 --> 00:15:12.662
Okay. And you're holding us why?

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.795
He's being held on suspicion of murder.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.565
- And you? We'll see.
- Murder?

00:15:17.568 --> 00:15:20.135
You sound genuinely surprised.

00:15:20.778 --> 00:15:22.275
Or are you that good of an actor?

00:15:22.289 --> 00:15:23.832
Who is he supposed to have murdered?

00:15:23.838 --> 00:15:26.044
- We'll get around to that.
- You can't just hold us here

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:29.334
- without formal charges.
- Actually, we can for 48 hours.

00:15:29.337 --> 00:15:31.894
But you, being a prelaw student,
would know that.

00:15:33.378 --> 00:15:34.935
I know all about you, Sam.

00:15:36.229 --> 00:15:37.625
You're 23 years old.

00:15:37.827 --> 00:15:39.613
No job, no home address.

00:15:40.637 --> 00:15:42.534
Your mother died when you were a baby.

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:45.504
Your father's whereabouts are unknown.

00:15:45.679 --> 00:15:47.025
And then there's

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:48.635
the case of your brother, Dean,

00:15:49.418 --> 00:15:52.213
whose demise was, well,
just a little bit exaggerated.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:54.283
Feel free to jump in whenever you like.

00:15:56.557 --> 00:15:57.614
Shy?

00:15:57.619 --> 00:15:58.745
No problem.

00:15:58.747 --> 00:15:59.774
I'll keep going.

00:16:00.207 --> 00:16:02.625
Your family moved around a lot
when you were a kid.

00:16:02.738 --> 00:16:05.433
Despite that, you were a straight-A student.

00:16:05.548 --> 00:16:08.043
Got into Stanford with a full ride.

00:16:11.128 --> 00:16:12.645
Then about a year ago,

00:16:12.648 --> 00:16:14.352
there was a fire in your apartment.

00:16:14.358 --> 00:16:15.725
One fatality...

00:16:15.727 --> 00:16:16.943
Jessica Moore,

00:16:17.089 --> 00:16:18.195
your girlfriend.

00:16:18.998 --> 00:16:23.155
After she died, you fell off the grid,
left behind everything.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:24.974
I needed some time off...

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.533
to deal.

00:16:28.539 --> 00:16:31.424
So I'm taking a road trip with my brother.

00:16:31.428 --> 00:16:33.864
- How's that going for you?
- Great.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.183
I mean...

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.674
we saw the second-largest ball of twine
in the continental US.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.794
Awesome.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:47.343
We ran Dean's fingerprints through iafis.

00:16:47.828 --> 00:16:50.683
Got over a dozen possible hits.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.385
"Possible" hits, which makes them worthless.

00:16:53.387 --> 00:16:54.775
But makes you wonder,

00:16:55.048 --> 00:16:57.525
what are we gonna find
when we run your prints?

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:59.415
Yeah, well, uh...

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.922
you be sure to let me know, all right?

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:03.543
May I?

00:17:03.607 --> 00:17:05.203
- Please.
- Great.

00:17:11.557 --> 00:17:13.643
Sam, you seem like a good kid.

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.913
It's not your fault Dean's your brother.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:17.785
We can't pick our family.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.912
Right now detectives in St. Louis
are exhuming a corpse.

00:17:21.918 --> 00:17:25.003
They're trying to figure out
how your brother faked his own death

00:17:25.168 --> 00:17:27.642
after torturing all those young women.

00:17:27.839 --> 00:17:29.615
Dean's a bad guy.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:31.195
His life is over.

00:17:31.758 --> 00:17:33.604
Yours doesn't have to be.

00:17:35.767 --> 00:17:38.203
You want me to turn against my own brother?

00:17:38.217 --> 00:17:41.195
No.
We already caught him cold,

00:17:41.569 --> 00:17:44.524
red-handed at the Karen Giles murder scene.

00:17:46.039 --> 00:17:48.102
We just need you

00:17:48.267 --> 00:17:50.153
to fill in some missing pieces.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.683
Why would I do that?

00:17:56.047 --> 00:17:58.402
Because I can talk to the D.A.,

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.995
make a deal for you.

00:18:00.378 --> 00:18:02.134
You can get on with your life.

00:18:02.839 --> 00:18:04.533
Dean's as good as gone.

00:18:11.199 --> 00:18:14.145
My dad and Tony Giles were old friends.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.312
They were in the service together.

00:18:17.319 --> 00:18:20.032
We've known him since we were kids,
you know?

00:18:21.249 --> 00:18:23.812
So we came as soon as we heard
about his death.

00:18:28.697 --> 00:18:30.253
Here you go.

00:18:30.847 --> 00:18:33.393
- Anthony Giles.
- Who's Anthony Giles?

00:18:33.657 --> 00:18:35.524
The Baltimore lawyer.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.303
Working late at office. Check it out.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:43.032
"His throat was slit but the room was clean"

00:18:44.008 --> 00:18:46.863
- Huh. No dna, no prints.
- Keep reading. It gets better.

00:18:47.089 --> 00:18:50.394
"Security cameras failed to capture footage
of the assailant"

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:52.943
Either somebody tampered with the tapes...

00:18:52.947 --> 00:18:54.423
or it's an invisible killer.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.055
My favorite kind.

00:18:56.478 --> 00:18:57.944
What do you think, Scully?
We check it out?

00:18:57.949 --> 00:18:59.673
I'm not Scully. You're Scully.

00:19:00.217 --> 00:19:01.155
No, I'm Mulder.

00:19:01.588 --> 00:19:02.822
You're a redheaded woman.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:04.564
So...

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.914
It would've been hard for Dean
to kill Tony,

00:19:07.917 --> 00:19:10.053
considering we weren't in town
at the time.

00:19:10.057 --> 00:19:11.583
So, tell me what happened next.

00:19:11.787 --> 00:19:13.134
Okay, uh,

00:19:13.479 --> 00:19:15.142
that's when we went to see Karen.

00:19:15.458 --> 00:19:17.225
She was barely holding it together.

00:19:17.719 --> 00:19:19.865
We just wanted to be there for her,
you know?

00:19:22.097 --> 00:19:23.825
Insurance.

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:27.063
I totally forgot about the insurance.

00:19:28.257 --> 00:19:30.123
We're very sorry to bother you
right now, but

00:19:31.147 --> 00:19:34.144
the company is required
to conduct its own investigation.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.912
- You understand?
- Sure.

00:19:37.109 --> 00:19:38.772
If you could just tell us anything

00:19:38.778 --> 00:19:40.815
you remember about the night
your husband died.

00:19:41.787 --> 00:19:43.622
Tony and I were supposed to have dinner.

00:19:43.629 --> 00:19:46.652
He called and said that he was having
computer troubles

00:19:47.003 --> 00:19:48.748
and that he had to work late.

00:19:50.221 --> 00:19:51.729
That was it.

00:19:52.834 --> 00:19:55.598
Do you have any idea
who could've done this to him?

00:19:56.191 --> 00:19:59.544
No. It's like i told the police. I...

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:01.334
I have no idea.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:02.982
Did Tony mention anything

00:20:02.987 --> 00:20:04.363
unusual

00:20:04.609 --> 00:20:06.872
to you in the days before his death?

00:20:07.689 --> 00:20:09.013
Unusual?

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.453
Yeah, like strange.

00:20:13.568 --> 00:20:15.702
- Strange?
- You know, Karen, weird.

00:20:15.859 --> 00:20:17.583
Weird noises,

00:20:17.927 --> 00:20:20.023
visions, anything like that?

00:20:26.777 --> 00:20:29.764
He had a nightmare the day before he died.

00:20:30.417 --> 00:20:32.483
What kind of a nightmare?

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:35.553
Uh, he said that he woke up
in the middle of the night,

00:20:35.557 --> 00:20:38.012
and there was a woman standing at
the foot of the bed.

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:42.103
He blinked. She was gone.
I mean, it was just a nightmare.

00:20:43.039 --> 00:20:44.553
Did he say what she looked like?

00:20:46.488 --> 00:20:49.204
What the helle difference does it make
what she looked like?!

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:55.385
Uh, it's just our company is very thorough.

00:20:56.928 --> 00:20:59.615
He said she was pale,
and she had dark, red eyes.

00:21:00.958 --> 00:21:02.463
So I gave Karen a hug,

00:21:03.349 --> 00:21:05.443
told her to call me
if she needed anything, and

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:07.072
that was it.

00:21:07.917 --> 00:21:09.075
End of story.

00:21:10.879 --> 00:21:13.323
Sam, I am trying to help you here,

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:16.113
but you have got to be honest with me.

00:21:17.087 --> 00:21:19.092
Now, we have an eyewitness,

00:21:19.307 --> 00:21:21.402
someone who saw two men

00:21:21.807 --> 00:21:25.232
fitting your and your brother's description
breaking into Giles' office.

00:21:25.239 --> 00:21:26.282
Ok, look,

00:21:26.508 --> 00:21:29.885
Karen called us later, said that there was
some stuff she wanted from Tony's office,

00:21:29.888 --> 00:21:31.554
but the police weren't letting her in.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.354
Like a picture of the two of them in Paris
and some other stuff.

00:21:35.659 --> 00:21:37.945
Look, it was wrong to enter a crime scene,
but

00:21:37.948 --> 00:21:39.382
she gave us the key.

00:21:52.319 --> 00:21:53.254
Hey.

00:21:53.949 --> 00:21:56.514
Anthony Giles' body was found
right about here.

00:21:57.227 --> 00:21:58.893
"Throat slit so deep,"

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:00.635
"that part of his spinal cord was visible".

00:22:02.218 --> 00:22:03.532
What do you think?

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:04.953
Vengeful spirit?

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:07.242
- Underline "vengeful"?
- Yeah. Maybe.

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:10.523
I mean, he did see that woman
at the foot of his bed.

00:22:14.828 --> 00:22:16.174
Look at this.

00:22:19.269 --> 00:22:20.543
"danashulps"

00:22:21.367 --> 00:22:23.022
What's that, a name?

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:26.314
I don't know, but it's everywhere.

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:32.662
"All work and no play makes Jack
a dull boy"

00:22:53.158 --> 00:22:56.073
I'd say we've officially crossed over
into weird.

00:22:56.319 --> 00:22:57.635
Maybe Giles knew her.

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.435
Maybe it's the name of our pale,
red-eyed mystery girl.

00:23:00.657 --> 00:23:01.754
Well...

00:23:02.569 --> 00:23:04.203
let's see what we can see.

00:23:10.269 --> 00:23:12.564
There's not a single mention of
a Dana Shulps anywhere.

00:23:13.038 --> 00:23:14.303
There's not a D. Shulps

00:23:14.307 --> 00:23:15.844
or any other kind of freaking Shulps.

00:23:15.850 --> 00:23:16.833
Great.

00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:18.404
- What do you got?
- Nothing.

00:23:18.407 --> 00:23:23.172
No Dana Shulps has ever lived or died
in Baltimore in the last 50 years at least.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:25.025
- So, what now?
- Well,

00:23:25.029 --> 00:23:27.125
I think I'm pretty close
to cracking Giles' password.

00:23:27.129 --> 00:23:28.993
Maybe there's something
in his personal files, you know.

00:23:28.997 --> 00:23:30.304
By "close" you mean...

00:23:30.659 --> 00:23:31.843
30 minutes maybe.

00:23:34.507 --> 00:23:35.594
Awesome.

00:23:37.179 --> 00:23:39.002
So, I guess I just get to, uh,

00:23:39.538 --> 00:23:40.752
hang out.

00:23:40.879 --> 00:23:41.872
That's

00:23:41.927 --> 00:23:42.942
awesome.

00:23:56.929 --> 00:23:58.084
Dude, seriously.

00:23:58.090 --> 00:23:59.664
Alright. I'm gonna go talk to Karen again,

00:23:59.668 --> 00:24:01.802
see if she knows anything about
this Dana Shulps, huh?

00:24:02.088 --> 00:24:02.855
Great.

00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:05.233
Keep going, sparky.

00:24:06.799 --> 00:24:09.472
Then Dean went back to Karen's place
to check up on her.

00:24:09.610 --> 00:24:10.592
I mean,

00:24:10.848 --> 00:24:12.863
you know,
she had been pretty upset earlier.

00:24:12.879 --> 00:24:14.482
So why didn't you go with him?

00:24:15.759 --> 00:24:17.733
I just went back to the motel.

00:24:18.917 --> 00:24:20.885
How did you know I was there,
by the way?

00:24:21.327 --> 00:24:24.834
We found the motel matchbook on your brother
when we arrested him.

00:24:27.068 --> 00:24:28.812
Let's quit fooling around.

00:24:29.247 --> 00:24:32.052
Now, you were with your brother
the whole time you were in Baltimore.

00:24:32.057 --> 00:24:34.065
Why separate now?

00:24:34.318 --> 00:24:36.785
Because your brother left you
to go murder Karen.

00:24:36.789 --> 00:24:40.705
- He didn't kill anyone.
- I heard the 911 call!

00:24:40.709 --> 00:24:44.424
Karen was terrified!
She said someone was in the house.

00:25:53.687 --> 00:25:56.184
<i>- Emergency services.</i>
- Hello?

00:25:56.187 --> 00:25:58.172
I think I saw somebody in my house.

00:25:58.180 --> 00:25:59.513
<i>What is your address, ma'am?

00:25:59.518 --> 00:26:01.513
It's 421 Clinton avenue.

00:26:02.448 --> 00:26:03.602
Please...

00:26:04.350 --> 00:26:05.212
Hello?

00:26:58.428 --> 00:26:59.634
Karen, are you in there?

00:27:52.640 --> 00:27:53.745
Oh, god.

00:28:06.948 --> 00:28:08.462
Seriously, what the hell?

00:28:27.327 --> 00:28:28.572
Freeze.

00:28:28.759 --> 00:28:29.875
Stay on your knees.

00:28:30.408 --> 00:28:31.803
Hands where I can see them.

00:28:32.178 --> 00:28:33.202
Now!

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.152
Cuff him.

00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:50.504
You getting anywhere with him?

00:28:50.779 --> 00:28:51.665
No.

00:28:52.189 --> 00:28:54.175
Just a lot of wise ass remarks.

00:28:54.179 --> 00:28:55.185
You?

00:28:55.899 --> 00:28:58.695
Sam's story matches Dean's
to the last detail.

00:28:59.870 --> 00:29:02.085
Yeah, well, these guys are good.

00:29:02.458 --> 00:29:03.633
I'll give them that.

00:29:05.668 --> 00:29:09.703
If we don't get Sam to flip, we have nothing
but a lot of circumstantial evidence.

00:29:09.717 --> 00:29:13.002
We got Dean at the crime scene
with blood on his hands.

00:29:13.367 --> 00:29:15.394
Juries have convicted for less.

00:29:15.977 --> 00:29:18.865
Yeah, but, I mean,
where is the murder weapon?

00:29:19.280 --> 00:29:21.835
What's the motive?
You talk about reasonable doubt.

00:29:21.839 --> 00:29:22.604
Diana...

00:29:23.887 --> 00:29:24.822
do you

00:29:24.900 --> 00:29:26.054
have reasonable doubt?

00:29:31.478 --> 00:29:34.425
We keep leaning on these guys,
one of them will tumble.

00:29:34.430 --> 00:29:36.395
And don't forget about St. Louis.

00:29:37.469 --> 00:29:38.334
I'm telling you,

00:29:38.417 --> 00:29:39.624
this Dean guy

00:29:39.628 --> 00:29:40.645
is our guy.

00:29:41.817 --> 00:29:44.002
I know Tony Giles was a friend of yours.

00:29:44.007 --> 00:29:45.932
Yeah, he was. He was a good friend.

00:29:45.940 --> 00:29:48.625
I know you want to clean this mess up quick,

00:29:49.108 --> 00:29:51.853
but come on.
Tony knew a lot of criminal types.

00:29:51.859 --> 00:29:54.394
- Maybe we just...
- "Criminal types"?

00:29:55.048 --> 00:29:59.004
He was a defense lawyer, for god sakes.
Of course he knew criminal types.

00:29:59.998 --> 00:30:01.012
Okay.

00:30:01.398 --> 00:30:03.972
- All right. Let's get back at them.
- No. You know what?

00:30:04.169 --> 00:30:06.324
Let them stew in their juices for a bit.

00:30:12.640 --> 00:30:13.892
Come here.

00:30:29.350 --> 00:30:32.475
Dana Shulps, Dana Shulps,
Dana Shulps...

00:30:42.719 --> 00:30:44.373
Maybe it's not a name.

00:30:45.168 --> 00:30:47.003
Maybe it's not a name?

00:30:47.819 --> 00:30:49.324
Anagram maybe?

00:31:05.927 --> 00:31:06.952
Mr. Winchester?

00:31:07.109 --> 00:31:07.932
Yeah.

00:31:08.139 --> 00:31:09.492
I'm Jeff Crouse.

00:31:10.438 --> 00:31:12.584
I'm with the public defender's office.

00:31:13.787 --> 00:31:15.035
I'm your lawyer.

00:31:15.487 --> 00:31:18.024
Oh, thank god. I'm saved.

00:31:19.579 --> 00:31:22.022
Can I, uh, steal a pen from you
and some paper?

00:31:22.030 --> 00:31:22.824
Sure.

00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:25.805
Well,

00:31:25.809 --> 00:31:26.624
the

00:31:26.628 --> 00:31:28.472
police haven't found a weapon yet.

00:31:29.009 --> 00:31:30.175
So that's good.

00:31:30.920 --> 00:31:31.902
But, uh,

00:31:31.907 --> 00:31:33.383
they got your prints

00:31:33.777 --> 00:31:35.263
and literally

00:31:36.098 --> 00:31:37.833
blood on your hands. And

00:31:38.708 --> 00:31:39.875
with your police record...

00:31:43.080 --> 00:31:44.454
Mr. Winchester,

00:31:44.880 --> 00:31:47.432
- what are you doing?
- I think it's an anagram.

00:31:47.738 --> 00:31:51.104
- A what?
- An anagram. Same letters, different words.

00:31:52.790 --> 00:31:54.043
Could you do me a favor?

00:31:54.769 --> 00:31:57.014
See if you recognize any
of these words, you know.

00:31:57.019 --> 00:31:59.444
Local names, places, anything like that.

00:32:00.659 --> 00:32:03.224
Do you understand how serious
these charges are?

00:32:04.797 --> 00:32:07.015
I'm handcuffed to a table. Yeah. I get it.

00:32:07.098 --> 00:32:09.304
Humor me. Take a quick look.

00:32:16.698 --> 00:32:19.134
Well, S-U-P?
I don't know about that, but...

00:32:20.468 --> 00:32:21.803
Ashland is

00:32:21.809 --> 00:32:23.295
is a street name.

00:32:23.568 --> 00:32:25.065
It's not far from here.

00:32:25.070 --> 00:32:25.943
Street?

00:32:27.940 --> 00:32:31.844
Let's start with where you were
the night that Anthony Giles died.

00:32:31.850 --> 00:32:33.414
Can you get in to see my brother?

00:32:33.420 --> 00:32:34.892
Mr. Winchester...

00:32:35.740 --> 00:32:38.204
you could be facing
the death penalty here.

00:32:38.410 --> 00:32:40.555
Hey, thanks for the law review, Matlock.

00:32:41.110 --> 00:32:43.145
But if you want to help me...

00:32:46.017 --> 00:32:47.822
I need you to see my brother.

00:33:31.620 --> 00:33:32.995
I hope that was meaningful.

00:33:34.197 --> 00:33:36.333
But I'd like to discuss your case now.

00:33:37.047 --> 00:33:38.553
Sure thing, Matlock.

00:33:39.629 --> 00:33:41.804
You two really are brothers, aren't you?

00:33:42.560 --> 00:33:43.523
Now...

00:33:44.379 --> 00:33:45.505
as you know,

00:33:46.170 --> 00:33:48.413
the D.A. might be interested in...

00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:52.912
We need you with the other one.

00:34:00.798 --> 00:34:02.433
This should be nice.

00:34:06.520 --> 00:34:07.594
Counselor...

00:34:08.770 --> 00:34:10.443
your boy decided to confess.

00:34:10.569 --> 00:34:11.904
Mr. Winchester,

00:34:12.589 --> 00:34:14.524
I would advise against that strongly.

00:34:14.557 --> 00:34:16.332
Talk directly into the camera.

00:34:16.340 --> 00:34:18.225
Start by stating your name for the record.

00:34:22.140 --> 00:34:23.912
My name is Dean Winchester.

00:34:24.678 --> 00:34:25.973
I'm an aquarius.

00:34:25.978 --> 00:34:28.683
I enjoy sunsets, long walks on the beach,

00:34:28.689 --> 00:34:30.052
and frisky women.

00:34:30.850 --> 00:34:32.472
And I did not kill anyone,

00:34:33.119 --> 00:34:34.462
but I know who did.

00:34:34.469 --> 00:34:36.035
Or rather what did.

00:34:36.649 --> 00:34:38.095
Of course, it can't be for sure

00:34:38.100 --> 00:34:40.054
because our investigation was interrupted.

00:34:40.917 --> 00:34:42.212
But our working theory

00:34:42.307 --> 00:34:43.854
is that we're looking for some kind of

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:45.684
vengeful spirit.

00:34:45.930 --> 00:34:47.194
Excuse me?

00:34:47.659 --> 00:34:49.523
You know, Casper, the bloodthirsty ghost.

00:34:51.338 --> 00:34:52.524
Tony Giles saw it.

00:34:52.840 --> 00:34:55.005
I'll bet you cash money Karen did, too.

00:34:55.100 --> 00:34:57.603
See, the interesting thing is the word
it leaves behind.

00:34:57.607 --> 00:34:58.572
For some reason,

00:34:58.578 --> 00:35:00.083
it's trying to tell us something.

00:35:01.170 --> 00:35:03.065
But communicating across a veil

00:35:03.787 --> 00:35:04.814
ain't easy.

00:35:05.430 --> 00:35:07.902
And sometimes the spirits,
they get things jumbled.

00:35:08.318 --> 00:35:09.492
You remember "Redrum".

00:35:10.050 --> 00:35:10.982
Same concept.

00:35:11.589 --> 00:35:12.443
You know,

00:35:12.970 --> 00:35:14.372
it could be word fragments.

00:35:14.598 --> 00:35:15.762
Other times...

00:35:19.278 --> 00:35:20.133
It's anagrams.

00:35:21.230 --> 00:35:23.462
See, at first we thought
this was a name, Dana Shulps.

00:35:24.788 --> 00:35:25.643
But now

00:35:25.988 --> 00:35:27.372
we think it's a street.

00:35:27.378 --> 00:35:28.383
Ashland.

00:35:28.579 --> 00:35:29.953
Whatever is going on,

00:35:31.038 --> 00:35:34.664
- I'm betting it started there.
- You arrogant bastard.

00:35:35.358 --> 00:35:38.212
Tony and Karen were good people,
and you're making jokes.

00:35:38.217 --> 00:35:39.834
I'm not joking, Ponch.

00:35:41.829 --> 00:35:45.882
You murdered them in cold blood
just like that girl in St. Louis.

00:35:45.890 --> 00:35:47.415
Oh, yeah, that wasn't me, either.

00:35:47.419 --> 00:35:50.045
That was a shapeshifter creature
that only looked like me.

00:35:53.690 --> 00:35:55.134
Pete, that is enough!

00:35:56.947 --> 00:35:58.024
You asked for the truth.

00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:02.304
Lock this guy off.

00:36:15.249 --> 00:36:16.432
What the hell?

00:36:18.239 --> 00:36:19.505
Where is he?

00:36:28.829 --> 00:36:29.644
How did he do it?

00:36:30.487 --> 00:36:31.973
The fire escape's way over...

00:36:34.157 --> 00:36:36.303
- What?
- These two guys.

00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:41.592
Hilts and Mcqueen?

00:36:41.988 --> 00:36:42.852
What is that?

00:36:42.910 --> 00:36:45.515
Hilts is Steve Mcqueen's character in
"The Great Escape".

00:37:43.748 --> 00:37:45.263
Can we make this quick?

00:37:45.380 --> 00:37:48.074
I'm really tired.
It's been a long day, you know,

00:37:48.077 --> 00:37:49.693
with your partner assaulting me and all.

00:37:49.988 --> 00:37:52.074
I want to know more about that stuff

00:37:52.078 --> 00:37:54.515
- you were talking about earlier.
- Time life,

00:37:54.698 --> 00:37:56.174
"mysteries of the unknown".

00:37:56.380 --> 00:37:57.595
Look it up.

00:38:02.339 --> 00:38:04.374
Let's pretend for the moment

00:38:04.897 --> 00:38:07.065
you're not entirely insane.

00:38:07.910 --> 00:38:11.754
What would one of these things
be doing here?

00:38:11.760 --> 00:38:13.415
Vengeful spirit?

00:38:16.189 --> 00:38:18.823
Well, they're created by violent deaths,

00:38:19.120 --> 00:38:21.975
and then they come back for a reason,
usually a nasty one,

00:38:21.980 --> 00:38:24.145
like revenge on the people that hurt them.

00:38:25.169 --> 00:38:27.065
And, uh, these

00:38:27.278 --> 00:38:28.735
spirits...

00:38:29.769 --> 00:38:32.053
They're capable of killing people.

00:38:37.300 --> 00:38:38.734
Where did you get that?

00:38:44.679 --> 00:38:45.603
I don't know.

00:38:47.387 --> 00:38:48.564
It wasn't there before.

00:38:50.437 --> 00:38:51.914
You've seen it, haven't you?

00:38:52.807 --> 00:38:53.694
The spirit.

00:38:53.807 --> 00:38:54.904
How did you know?

00:38:55.128 --> 00:38:57.572
Because Karen had the same bruises
on her wrists.

00:38:58.528 --> 00:39:01.543
I'm willing to bet that if you look at
Giles' autopsy photos, he's got them, too.

00:39:01.550 --> 00:39:03.165
It's got something to do with the spirit.

00:39:03.488 --> 00:39:04.885
I don't know what.

00:39:09.589 --> 00:39:10.365
I know.

00:39:11.578 --> 00:39:12.854
You think you're going crazy.

00:39:13.449 --> 00:39:15.093
But let's skip that part, shall we?

00:39:16.049 --> 00:39:18.315
Because the last two people
who saw this thing

00:39:18.738 --> 00:39:20.163
died pretty soon after.

00:39:22.279 --> 00:39:23.272
You hear me?

00:39:26.427 --> 00:39:28.093
You think I'm gonna die.

00:39:28.137 --> 00:39:29.434
You need to go to Sam.

00:39:30.628 --> 00:39:32.012
He'll help.

00:39:34.037 --> 00:39:35.574
You're giving your brother up.

00:39:36.027 --> 00:39:38.514
Go to the first motel listed
in the yellow pages.

00:39:38.689 --> 00:39:39.673
Look for Jim Rockford.

00:39:39.679 --> 00:39:41.455
That's how we find each other
when we're separated.

00:39:41.820 --> 00:39:43.254
You can arrest him, if you want.

00:39:44.069 --> 00:39:45.422
Or you can let him save your life.

00:40:03.378 --> 00:40:04.913
These showed up after you saw it?

00:40:05.078 --> 00:40:05.943
Yeah,

00:40:06.210 --> 00:40:07.844
- I guess.
- All right.

00:40:08.838 --> 00:40:10.985
You're gonna have to tell me
exactly what you saw.

00:40:12.139 --> 00:40:14.093
You know, I must be losing my mind.

00:40:15.658 --> 00:40:17.055
You're a fugitive.

00:40:17.107 --> 00:40:18.543
I should be arresting you.

00:40:18.547 --> 00:40:19.834
All right, well,

00:40:20.098 --> 00:40:22.114
you know what?
You can arrest me later, alright?

00:40:22.119 --> 00:40:23.473
After you live through this.

00:40:23.657 --> 00:40:25.593
But right now, you got to talk to me.

00:40:25.788 --> 00:40:26.945
Okay?

00:40:29.480 --> 00:40:30.493
Okay. Great.

00:40:30.767 --> 00:40:32.712
Now, the spirit, what did it look like?

00:40:32.717 --> 00:40:33.974
She was, um,

00:40:34.889 --> 00:40:36.143
really pale...

00:40:36.970 --> 00:40:38.622
and her throat was cut.

00:40:38.697 --> 00:40:41.505
And her eyes, they were like this deep,
dark red.

00:40:41.507 --> 00:40:44.115
It appeared like
she was trying to talk to me,

00:40:44.277 --> 00:40:45.755
but she couldn't.

00:40:46.559 --> 00:40:47.963
It was just...

00:40:47.967 --> 00:40:49.662
a lot of blood.

00:40:51.957 --> 00:40:53.434
You know what? Here.

00:40:53.438 --> 00:40:56.872
I've been researching every girl who has ever
died or gone missing from Ashland street.

00:40:59.177 --> 00:41:00.603
How did you get those?

00:41:00.610 --> 00:41:03.123
Those are from crime scenes
and booking photos.

00:41:04.118 --> 00:41:06.333
You have your job. I have mine.

00:41:07.268 --> 00:41:10.582
Here. I need you to look through these.
Tell me if you recognize anyone.

00:41:23.638 --> 00:41:24.715
This is her.

00:41:24.880 --> 00:41:25.953
I'm sure of it.

00:41:27.407 --> 00:41:28.593
Claire Becker?

00:41:29.269 --> 00:41:32.492
28 years old, disappeared about
eight or nine months ago.

00:41:32.499 --> 00:41:33.983
But I don't even know her.

00:41:33.987 --> 00:41:35.893
Why would she come after me?

00:41:35.898 --> 00:41:36.762
Well,

00:41:37.049 --> 00:41:39.695
before her death,
she was arrested twice

00:41:39.699 --> 00:41:40.892
for dealing heroin.

00:41:41.250 --> 00:41:42.964
- You ever work narcotics?
- Yeah,

00:41:42.970 --> 00:41:43.934
Pete and I did,

00:41:44.087 --> 00:41:45.394
before homicide.

00:41:46.067 --> 00:41:47.363
You ever bust her?

00:41:47.427 --> 00:41:48.802
Not that I remember.

00:41:52.307 --> 00:41:55.215
Says she was last seen entering
2911 Ashland street.

00:41:55.217 --> 00:41:56.752
Police searched the place,

00:41:57.280 --> 00:41:58.544
didn't find anything.

00:42:01.090 --> 00:42:02.532
Guess we got to check it out ourselves,

00:42:02.909 --> 00:42:04.202
see if we can find her body.

00:42:05.528 --> 00:42:06.285
What?

00:42:08.799 --> 00:42:10.585
Well, we got to salt and burn her bones.

00:42:11.018 --> 00:42:12.512
It's the only way to put her spirit to rest.

00:42:13.197 --> 00:42:14.414
Of course it is.

00:42:30.448 --> 00:42:32.584
So, what exactly are we looking for?

00:42:32.898 --> 00:42:34.515
I'll let you know when we find it.

00:43:29.338 --> 00:43:30.562
Sam!

00:43:40.888 --> 00:43:42.793
Hey, I'm here.
What is it?

00:43:43.119 --> 00:43:44.775
- What happened?
- Claire.

00:43:45.128 --> 00:43:46.764
- Where?
- She was here.

00:43:47.029 --> 00:43:48.053
Did she attack you?

00:43:48.400 --> 00:43:51.183
No. No, she was just like
reaching out to me.

00:43:51.617 --> 00:43:53.595
She was over there by the window.

00:44:05.780 --> 00:44:07.435
Here, help me move this.

00:44:08.348 --> 00:44:09.353
All right.

00:44:10.239 --> 00:44:11.364
I got it.

00:44:16.620 --> 00:44:18.375
Our little mystery word.

00:44:30.860 --> 00:44:32.715
Now the extra letters make sense.

00:44:38.340 --> 00:44:39.585
What is that?

00:44:41.028 --> 00:44:44.825
Spirits and certain remains
give off electromagnetic frequencies.

00:44:46.058 --> 00:44:48.255
So, if Claire's body was here,

00:44:48.708 --> 00:44:51.683
- that would indicate that?
- Yeah. Well, that's the theory.

00:45:17.119 --> 00:45:18.212
Yeah.

00:45:18.417 --> 00:45:20.714
Yeah, there's definitely something in there.

00:45:25.499 --> 00:45:26.765
You know,

00:45:27.599 --> 00:45:29.292
this is bothering me.

00:45:29.309 --> 00:45:31.434
Well, you are digging up a corpse.

00:45:31.438 --> 00:45:33.193
No, not that.

00:45:34.468 --> 00:45:36.665
That's, uh, pretty par for the course,
actually.

00:45:36.970 --> 00:45:38.305
Then what?

00:45:38.398 --> 00:45:39.222
It's just...

00:45:39.989 --> 00:45:43.483
I mean, no vengeful spirit
I've ever tussled with wanted to be wasted,

00:45:43.488 --> 00:45:46.513
so why the hell would Claire
lead us to her remains?

00:45:46.518 --> 00:45:48.255
Doesn't make any sense.

00:45:53.280 --> 00:45:54.354
All right. Here.

00:45:54.358 --> 00:45:55.344
Give me your hand.

00:46:30.300 --> 00:46:31.394
Her wrists.

00:46:32.110 --> 00:46:34.372
Yeah, they'd be bruised just like yours.

00:46:45.927 --> 00:46:47.482
That necklace mean something to you?

00:46:49.440 --> 00:46:50.635
I've seen it before.

00:46:52.550 --> 00:46:53.504
It's rare.

00:46:54.019 --> 00:46:56.194
It was custom-made over
on Carson street.

00:47:00.838 --> 00:47:02.265
I have one just like it.

00:47:04.058 --> 00:47:05.373
Pete gave it to me.

00:47:10.820 --> 00:47:12.475
Now this all makes perfect sense.

00:47:12.669 --> 00:47:13.655
I'm sorry?

00:47:13.657 --> 00:47:15.943
Yeah. You see,
Claire is not a vengeful spirit.

00:47:16.047 --> 00:47:17.303
She's a death omen.

00:47:18.079 --> 00:47:19.403
Excuse me?

00:47:19.659 --> 00:47:20.975
Claire's not killing anyone.

00:47:22.337 --> 00:47:23.562
She's trying to warn them.

00:47:25.888 --> 00:47:28.103
Sometimes spirits,
they don't want vengeance.

00:47:28.110 --> 00:47:30.814
They want justice, which is why
she led us here in the first place.

00:47:30.820 --> 00:47:32.945
She wants us to know who her killer is.

00:47:37.779 --> 00:47:40.322
Detective, how much do you know
about your partner?

00:47:43.670 --> 00:47:45.963
- Oh, my god.
- What?

00:47:47.539 --> 00:47:49.223
About a year ago,

00:47:49.408 --> 00:47:52.194
some heroin went missing from lockup.

00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:54.154
Obviously it was a cop.

00:47:54.848 --> 00:47:56.442
We never found out who did it.

00:47:57.880 --> 00:48:01.245
But whoever did it would need someone
to fence their product.

00:48:01.298 --> 00:48:02.692
Somebody like a heroin dealer.

00:48:04.728 --> 00:48:05.852
Somebody like Claire.

00:48:11.370 --> 00:48:13.913
So, I'm being extradited to St. Louis, huh?

00:48:16.899 --> 00:48:20.855
You just decided to transfer me yourself
800 miles at 2:00 in the morning?

00:48:25.938 --> 00:48:27.235
This can't be good.

00:48:28.048 --> 00:48:29.473
All right. Thanks.

00:48:30.219 --> 00:48:31.042
What is it?

00:48:31.227 --> 00:48:32.745
Pete just left the precinct.

00:48:32.977 --> 00:48:34.384
- With Dean.
- What?!

00:48:34.387 --> 00:48:37.793
He said the prisoner had to be transferred,
and he just took him.

00:48:37.797 --> 00:48:40.763
Dispatch has been calling,
but he won't answer the radio.

00:48:40.777 --> 00:48:41.843
Radio?

00:48:41.850 --> 00:48:43.922
- He took a county vehicle?
- Yeah.

00:48:43.927 --> 00:48:46.383
Then it should have a lojack.
You just got to get it turned on.

00:49:01.020 --> 00:49:02.002
Pee break?

00:49:02.069 --> 00:49:03.175
So soon?

00:49:03.840 --> 00:49:05.743
I think you might want
to get your prostate checked.

00:49:15.398 --> 00:49:16.784
Son of a bitch.

00:49:19.987 --> 00:49:22.364
Hey, I'm cool in the van.
You go do what you got to do.

00:49:27.559 --> 00:49:29.343
You're a cocky son of a bitch.

00:49:30.507 --> 00:49:33.734
You think those people in St. Louis
are gonna buy that crap you're paddling?

00:49:34.587 --> 00:49:35.942
Here's the thing.

00:49:36.469 --> 00:49:38.353
You're not gonna make it to St. Louis.

00:49:39.509 --> 00:49:40.734
You're gonna die

00:49:41.108 --> 00:49:42.442
trying to escape.

00:49:45.260 --> 00:49:46.594
Wait! Wait!

00:49:48.237 --> 00:49:49.473
Let's talk about this.

00:49:49.479 --> 00:49:51.312
You don't want to do something
that you're gonna regret.

00:49:53.078 --> 00:49:54.562
- Or maybe you do.
- Pete!

00:49:55.057 --> 00:49:56.183
Put the gun down.

00:49:56.449 --> 00:49:57.345
Diana?

00:49:58.187 --> 00:49:59.164
How'd you find me?

00:49:59.830 --> 00:50:01.093
I know about Claire.

00:50:01.097 --> 00:50:02.443
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:50:02.450 --> 00:50:04.275
Put the gun down!

00:50:04.279 --> 00:50:05.815
No, I don't think so.

00:50:06.528 --> 00:50:07.595
You're fast.

00:50:07.818 --> 00:50:09.553
Pretty sure I'm faster.

00:50:10.849 --> 00:50:11.863
Why are you doing this?

00:50:12.210 --> 00:50:13.734
I didn't do anything, Diana.

00:50:14.247 --> 00:50:15.673
It's a little late for that.

00:50:16.840 --> 00:50:18.182
It wasn't my fault.

00:50:19.077 --> 00:50:21.752
Claire was gonna turn me in.
I had no choice.

00:50:21.760 --> 00:50:22.824
And Tony?

00:50:23.197 --> 00:50:24.102
Karen?

00:50:24.208 --> 00:50:25.393
Same thing.

00:50:25.798 --> 00:50:28.204
Tony scrubbed the money.
Then he got skittish.

00:50:28.220 --> 00:50:30.022
And then he wanted to come clean.

00:50:30.027 --> 00:50:31.812
I'm sure he told Karen everything.

00:50:32.569 --> 00:50:34.705
It was a mess. I had to clean it up.

00:50:35.868 --> 00:50:36.923
I just panicked.

00:50:37.138 --> 00:50:39.513
How many more people
are gonna die over this, Pete?

00:50:39.520 --> 00:50:40.975
There's a way out.

00:50:42.517 --> 00:50:45.062
This Dean kid is a friggin' gift.

00:50:45.487 --> 00:50:47.465
We can pin the whole thing on him.

00:50:47.669 --> 00:50:51.752
Okay? No trial, nothing.
Just one more dead scumbag.

00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:52.713
Hey!

00:50:55.227 --> 00:50:56.503
No one will question it.

00:50:57.329 --> 00:50:59.165
Diana, please.

00:50:59.609 --> 00:51:00.993
I still love you.

00:51:07.397 --> 00:51:08.473
Thank you.

00:51:10.420 --> 00:51:11.554
Thank you.

00:51:20.877 --> 00:51:24.042
Then why don't you buy me another necklace,
you ass?

00:51:26.760 --> 00:51:28.872
Don't do it. Don't do it.

00:52:18.878 --> 00:52:19.963
You're doing all right?

00:52:21.160 --> 00:52:22.165
Not really.

00:52:23.429 --> 00:52:25.054
The death omen, Claire,

00:52:26.017 --> 00:52:27.413
what happens to her now?

00:52:27.607 --> 00:52:28.694
It should be over.

00:52:29.419 --> 00:52:30.783
She should be at rest.

00:52:32.518 --> 00:52:33.525
So, uh,

00:52:34.020 --> 00:52:35.372
what now, officer?

00:52:35.808 --> 00:52:37.415
Pete did confess to me.

00:52:37.520 --> 00:52:39.834
He screwed up both your cases royally.

00:52:39.910 --> 00:52:43.202
I'd say there's a good chance
that we can get your cases dismissed.

00:52:43.210 --> 00:52:45.842
- You could take care of that for us?
- I hope so.

00:52:46.039 --> 00:52:48.092
But the St. Louis murder charges?

00:52:48.380 --> 00:52:50.003
That's another story.

00:52:50.450 --> 00:52:52.115
I.. I can't help you.

00:52:53.708 --> 00:52:55.163
Unless

00:52:55.310 --> 00:52:58.163
I just happened to turn my back
and you walked away.

00:52:58.168 --> 00:53:00.305
I could tell them
that the suspects escaped.

00:53:00.438 --> 00:53:02.574
- Wait. Are you sure?
- Yeah, she's sure, Sam.

00:53:02.579 --> 00:53:05.435
You could lose your job over
something like that.

00:53:05.908 --> 00:53:08.543
Look, I just want you guys out there,
doing what you do best.

00:53:08.547 --> 00:53:09.444
Trust me.

00:53:09.687 --> 00:53:10.943
I'll sleep better at night.

00:53:12.077 --> 00:53:13.375
Listen, you need to watch your back.

00:53:13.390 --> 00:53:15.403
They're gonna be looking for both of you
right now.

00:53:16.359 --> 00:53:17.323
Get out of here.

00:53:17.827 --> 00:53:20.094
- I got to radio this in.
- Hey, uh...

00:53:20.578 --> 00:53:22.994
You wouldn't happen to know where
my car is by chance?

00:53:22.997 --> 00:53:25.793
It's at the impound yard on Robertson.

00:53:26.919 --> 00:53:28.004
Don't

00:53:28.170 --> 00:53:31.313
- even think about it.
- It's okay. It's all right. Don't worry.

00:53:31.588 --> 00:53:34.114
We'll just improvise.
We're pretty good at that.

00:53:34.117 --> 00:53:35.844
Yeah. I've noticed.

00:53:41.610 --> 00:53:43.483
- Nice lady.
- Yeah, for a cop.

00:53:44.527 --> 00:53:46.015
Did she look familiar to you?

00:53:46.020 --> 00:53:46.894
No. Why?

00:53:47.119 --> 00:53:49.093
I don't know. It's nothing.
Hey, you hungry?

00:53:49.099 --> 00:53:49.853
No.

00:53:49.860 --> 00:53:52.064
I have some reason
I could really go for some pea soup.



00:12:22.982 --> 00:12:24.482
